    "body": "Attendees: Keith, Anne, Philip, Simon, Emilio, Kagami, Mike, Olli\nScribe: Anne, Kagami\n\nBrief minutes:\n\n- Emilio: how to handle changes across multiple specifications?\n- Anne: stage them all, and ideally merge around the same time.\n\nAction items?\n- Simon: haven’t started on mine.\n\nAnything else?\n- Philip: about interesttarget. There’s going to be a CSS property that needs some infrastructure in HTML. Is there precedent for that?\n- Simon: innerText looks at the style system.\n- Emilio: you can’t look at the style at random times. Also need to be aware of dynamic changes.\n- [Some discussion about popovers.]\n- [Some discussion about Rust/Swift migration and lines of code of browsers]\n- https://github.com/whatwg/meta/issues/350\n  - [sideshowbarker] None of Flow, Servo, Ladybird are releasing anything to customers but not sure why that should be required\n  - [olli] because webcompat\n  - [anne] and to prevent toy project from influencing\n  - [simon] ladybird etc. are not even in beta and has webcompat issues so is disqualified\n  - [anne] we could file bugs on ladybird to help them or do other things to include them better perhaps\n  - [sideshowbarker] olli's argument makes sense, should be documented somewhere. The current situation is not affecting ladybird but maybe affecting other projects. Ladybird will do beta in a couple of years. Flow will not do public release but just doing embedded software.\n",
